"""Eight original MDS questions appended to the myeloid chapter."""
from create_aml import rows,q,EL,AP,OL,MR,QU
from qbank_authoring import ref
MD=ref('NCI: Myelodysplastic Syndromes Treatment—Health Professional PDQ','https://www.cancer.gov/types/myeloproliferative/hp/myelodysplastic-treatment-pdq')
IP=ref('NEJM Evidence: Molecular International Prognostic Scoring System for MDS','https://evidence.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/EVIDoa2200008')
IM=ref('US Prescribing Information: Imetelstat','https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/fda/fdaDrugXsl.cfm?setid=b0fab7ca-e578-43c5-9df6-bdaff4182257')
LU=ref('US Prescribing Information: Luspatercept','https://dailymed-beta.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/fda/fdaDrugXsl.cfm?setid=82f4d266-3f52-41eb-86ba-0abf3cf468e8&type=display')
q('Which combination best supports a diagnosis of MDS after appropriate exclusion of reversible mimics?', 'Persistent cytopenia with qualifying marrow dysplasia and/or defining clonal genetic findings in the relevant classification',[
 ('A single DNMT3A mutation with normal counts and no disease features','This can be clonal hematopoiesis rather than MDS.'),('One low platelet count during an acute infection','Transient cytopenia alone is insufficient.'),('Macrocytosis alone without further assessment','Many nutritional, drug and systemic causes exist.')],
 'MDS is an integrated neoplastic diagnosis', '**Cytopenia, morphology, blasts and genetic findings are interpreted together.**',['Exclude B12, folate, copper, medication and other mimics.','WHO and ICC contain genetic and morphological categories with specific criteria.'], '**Separate a clone from a defined neoplasm.**',['CHIP and CCUS are related but distinct concepts.','Persistent unexplained abnormalities justify appropriate marrow evaluation.'],[['Counts','Persistent cytopenia'],['Marrow','Dysplasia and blast assessment'],['Genetics','Clonality and defining alterations']],[MD])
q('What does IPSS-M add to MDS prognostic assessment?', 'Somatic mutation information integrated with clinical and cytogenetic variables',[
 ('Only the serum ferritin value','That is not the model’s defining addition.'),('A replacement for establishing the diagnosis','Prognostic scoring follows a correct disease diagnosis.'),('A guarantee of the same outcome for all patients in a group','Risk models estimate probabilities rather than certainty.')],
 'Molecular biology refines risk beyond a blood count alone', '**IPSS-M incorporates mutation data into prognostic stratification.**',['It can reclassify risk relative to older systems.','Blast percentage, cytopenias and cytogenetic features remain relevant.'], '**Use the model to support a clinical decision.**',['Fitness, transfusion burden and goals are not replaced by a score.','A risk estimate must be interpreted at the appropriate disease time point.'],[['Addition','Somatic mutation data'],['Integration','Clinical and cytogenetic factors'],['Use','Prognosis and treatment planning']],[IP])
q('An adult has lower-risk MDS with del(5q) and transfusion-dependent anemia. Which drug is an established disease-specific option?', 'Lenalidomide',[
 ('Imatinib without a BCR::ABL1 indication','That is not the matched del(5q) MDS strategy.'),('ATRA alone for all MDS','ATRA is not the defining treatment for this subtype.'),('Rifampicin as the marrow-directed treatment','This is an antimicrobial, not this neoplasm treatment.')],
 'A cytogenetic lesion can identify a specific anemia-treatment pathway', '**Lenalidomide can reduce transfusion dependence in suitable del(5q) MDS.**',['The full genetic and risk context matters.','TP53 abnormalities can influence prognosis and response durability.'], '**Monitor treatment-related cytopenias and other risks.**',['Use appropriate dose and renal assessment.','Continue evaluation for disease progression rather than judging only Hb response.'],[['Subtype','Lower-risk del(5q) MDS'],['Option','Lenalidomide'],['Monitoring','Counts, toxicity and disease course']],[MD],style='clinical_scenario')
q('Which mechanism explains luspatercept benefit in appropriate lower-risk MDS anemia?', 'Improved late-stage erythroid maturation',[
 ('Direct inhibition of BCR::ABL1','That is the CML TKI mechanism.'),('Selective destruction of all marrow stem cells','That is not its therapeutic action.'),('Direct replacement of lost iron stores','It is not iron supplementation.')],
 'Maturation support differs from stimulating early erythropoiesis alone', '**Luspatercept modulates TGF-beta-superfamily signaling.**',['Eligibility includes defined lower-risk MDS populations under current labeling.','The ESA-naive and post-ESA settings should be distinguished.'], '**Choose according to the exact anemia phenotype and evidence.**',['Ring sideroblast/SF3B1 biology and transfusion burden can be relevant.','Monitor Hb, blood pressure and treatment response.'],[['Action','Late erythroid maturation'],['Selection','Current label and risk context'],['Outcome','Anemia and transfusion-burden response']],[LU,MD])
q('What is the target of imetelstat in the labeled lower-risk MDS anemia setting?', 'Telomerase',[
 ('BCL2','That is the venetoclax target.'),('JAK2','That is targeted by selected MPN drugs.'),('CD38','That is targeted by selected plasma-cell therapies.')],
 'A newer anemia option has a distinct molecular mechanism', '**Imetelstat is an oligonucleotide telomerase inhibitor.**',['The US indication is defined by risk, transfusion burden and ESA response or eligibility.','It is not a universal treatment for every MDS subtype.'], '**Monitor for treatment-related cytopenias.**',['Neutropenia and thrombocytopenia can be clinically important.','Use the current label for dose holds and laboratory monitoring.'],[['Drug','Imetelstat'],['Target','Telomerase'],['Important safety','Myelosuppression']],[IM])
q('A fit patient has higher-risk MDS with progressive cytopenias and adverse biological features. Which principle is appropriate?', 'Early assessment for disease-modifying treatment and allogeneic transplantation rather than anemia support alone',[
 ('Treat every case only with vitamins regardless of the confirmed neoplasm','That does not address progression risk.'),('A platelet transfusion permanently cures the clone','It supplies temporary support.'),('Risk category has no role in the treatment strategy','It is central to balancing disease modification and supportive care.')],
 'Higher-risk disease requires a strategy directed at progression and survival', '**Hypomethylating therapy and transplant evaluation are important options.**',['Allogeneic transplantation can be potentially curative in selected patients.','Comorbidity and donor availability affect suitability.'], '**Provide supportive care throughout treatment.**',['Infection, bleeding and transfusion needs remain important.','Discuss goals and expected treatment burden explicitly.'],[['Higher risk','Progression-focused planning'],['Options','Disease-modifying therapy and HSCT assessment'],['Support','Ongoing infection and transfusion care']],[MD],style='clinical_scenario')
q('An asymptomatic older adult has a myeloid-associated mutation but normal blood counts and no diagnostic marrow neoplasm. Which category may apply?', 'Clonal hematopoiesis of indeterminate potential',[
 ('AML established by any mutation','AML requires the relevant disease criteria.'),('Severe aplastic anemia','Normal counts do not fit severe marrow failure.'),('MDS established without cytopenia or defining disease evidence','A clone alone is not enough in this generic setting.')],
 'Age-related clonality is not automatically overt leukemia', '**CHIP describes a clone without a defined hematological neoplasm in the appropriate setting.**',['Risk depends on mutation type, clone size and other features.','Some clones also associate with cardiovascular risk.'], '**Avoid both overdiagnosis and complete neglect.**',['Review counts and clinical changes over time.','New cytopenias can require a different assessment.'],[['Clone plus normal counts','CHIP may apply'],['Clone plus unexplained cytopenia','CCUS is a separate consideration'],['Defined neoplasm','Requires its criteria']],[MD,IP],style='clinical_scenario')
q('Why should an MDS diagnosis not be based on ring sideroblasts alone?', 'Reversible toxic or nutritional disorders can also produce them, and modern categories integrate genetics and other criteria',[
 ('Ring sideroblasts are always normal marrow cells','They are an abnormal iron-distribution finding.'),('Every ring sideroblast proves AML','It does not define acute leukemia.'),('SF3B1 and the rest of the marrow assessment are irrelevant','They can be important to classification and prognosis.')],
 'A characteristic morphology still needs a cause', '**Alcohol, copper deficiency and selected medicines can create sideroblastic patterns.**',['The whole cytopenia and dysplasia assessment matters.','Modern SF3B1-related categories have specific diagnostic conditions.'], '**Correct reversible causes and apply a named classification.**',['Avoid unnecessary neoplasm treatment for a nutritional mimic.','Persistent clonal disease requires its own risk and treatment assessment.'],[['Morphology','Ring sideroblasts'],['Alternatives','Reversible acquired causes'],['Classification','Integrated genetic and marrow criteria']],[MD])
